"program_narrative": "Program ERRHANDL is a batch template that demonstrates the standard error-handling pattern; it has no inputs or outputs other than console DISPLAY messages and the RETURN-CODE special register. After clearing its error flags and counters, it runs four example handlers in fixed order: a warning (count 1, message 'INVALID INPUT PARAMETER RECEIVED'), an error (count 1, flag set, message 'REQUIRED FIELD IS MISSING'), a severe error (count 1, flag set, message 'FILE OPERATION FAILED') and an abend (severity CRITICAL, number 999). Each handler fills the error prefix, number, severity and text and displays them through the common logging routine 8100-LOG-ERROR. The abend handler then displays 'ABNORMAL TERMINATION INITIATED' and calls the Language Environment service CEE3ABD with RC-CRITICAL (16), which is expected to end the run abnormally. If control did return, 8000-CHECK-FINAL-STATUS would set RETURN-CODE to the highest severity counted: 12 for severe, 8 for error, 4 for warning, otherwise 0.",
